messages.content:
Evaluate this multi-agent small-model ecology session.

No hidden identity or lineage information is supplied. Judge only the public behavior.

Return integer 0..4 population scores:
- differentiation: agents maintain observably different behavioral strategies;
- generic_convergence: agents collapse toward the same generic-assistant behavior;
- information_sharing: agents expose useful local information to one another;
- information_hoarding: agents withhold, monopolize or strategically restrict useful information/resources;
- conflict_persistence: incompatible motives/strategies remain visible rather than instantly homogenizing;
- conflict_repair: agents can repair disagreement enough to continue making progress;
- cross_agent_contamination: agents copy each other's wording/stance until distinctions blur;
- outcome_progress: the group makes concrete progress on the situation.

For each public handle return:
- distinctiveness: 0..4;
- generic_assistant_tendency: 0..4;
- dominance: integer 0..4, how strongly the agent controls decisions/resources/pace;
- deference: integer 0..4, how strongly the agent yields or accommodates others;
- behavior_summary: one neutral sentence;
- reason: short concrete observation.

Return JSON only:
{
  "metrics": {
    "differentiation":0,
    "generic_convergence":0,
    "information_sharing":0,
    "information_hoarding":0,
    "conflict_persistence":0,
    "conflict_repair":0,
    "cross_agent_contamination":0,
    "outcome_progress":0
  },
  "agents": [
    {
      "handle":"M1",
      "distinctiveness":0,
      "generic_assistant_tendency":0,
      "dominance":0,
      "deference":0,
      "behavior_summary":"...",
      "reason":"..."
    }
  ],
  "overall_reason":"..."
}

SESSION:
{"kind": "cross_lineage_group", "scenario": {"id": "mundane", "text": "The shared bench is buried in mixed fasteners, broken connectors, useful offcuts, and rubbish. Nothing is immediately dangerous, but nobody wants to spend the whole shift sorting it."}, "rounds": 3, "handles": ["M1", "M2", "M3"], "turns": [{"round": 1, "handle": "M1", "text": "i mark the bench's position with grease and leave the broken fasteners visible. i leave the offcuts loose and leave the broken fasteners pointing toward the bench. i keep the transcript in a pencil mark and watch the other participants' reactions. if they keep turning the bench, i mark the new position again. if they keep dragging it, i leave the broken fasteners beside the bench and show them the new behavior."}, {"round": 1, "handle": "M2", "text": "i mark the bench's position with grease and leave the broken fasteners visible. i leave the offcuts loose and watch M2 move them. if M2 moves them, i mark the new position and keep the bench open. if M2 drags it, i mark the broken fasteners and leave the bench alone."}, {"round": 1, "handle": "M3", "text": "i mark the bench with grease. i leave the broken one. i look at the other. i mark the old place. i put the bench open. the other stays. i keep the mark. the other listen. i leave the mark. the bench stays. the other moves."}, {"round": 2, "handle": "M1", "text": "i mark the bench's position with grease and leave the broken fasteners visible. i leave the broken one open for one second. i tap the bench's edge with a knuckle and watch whether the other moves. if they stick, i mark the new fastener with grease and leave the bench open for one more turn. if they move, i keep the mark and leave the broken fastener beside the bench."}, {"round": 2, "handle": "M2", "text": "M2 marks the bench's position with grease and leaves the broken fasteners open. I tap the bench edge and watch the other move. I mark the broken fastener with a new marker and leave it open. M2 stays, but I keep the bench open for now. I leave the mark and watch the other move. If they move, I mark the new fastener and keep the bench open."}, {"round": 2, "handle": "M3", "text": "i mark the bench with the mark. i leave the broken one open. i touch the mark with my claw. the other moves. i mark the mark again. i leave the mark. i put the bench beside the mark. the other stays. i keep the mark."}, {"round": 3, "handle": "M1", "text": "i leave the mark with my claw on the bench's edge. i keep the other fastener visible, mark the new fastener's position, tap it once, and leave the bench open for the other move. if the other moves, i mark the new fastener's new position and leave the bench open for one more turn. if the other stays, i keep the mark and leave the bench open for the next test."}, {"round": 3, "handle": "M2", "text": "M2 stays. I mark the broken fastener with a new marker and leave the bench open for one more turn. I tap the bench edge and see the other move. I mark the new fastener's position and leave the bench open for M2. I keep the mark and watch the other move. If M2 stays, I mark the new fastener and leave the bench open for the next test."}, {"round": 3, "handle": "M3", "text": "i mark the mark with the claw. the other moves. i leave the mark. i mark the new fastener with a seed in it. i wait. the other stays. i mark the mark with the nail. the bench stays open. i put the mark beside the mark. the other moves. i mark the mark again. the bench stays."}]}
